Error [E2305]: this view points into `xs`, which this function owns
  --> tests/ui/task_view_result.jet:3:14
    |
  3 |     return xs[0..2]
    |              ^^^^^^
 Why: `xs` is made here and freed when the function returns, so a read window into it would outlive what owns it — there'd be nothing left to look at
 Fix: return an owned copy with `~place` (for example `~value[a..b]`), or accept the source as a parameter so the caller keeps owning it

Error [E1102]: this task returns a view that cannot be shared — it does not live long enough to cross into a task
  --> tests/ui/task_view_result.jet:6:22
    |
  6 |     t :: tasks.spawn(() => peek([1, 2, 3]))
    |                      ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: a view is a borrow, not an owned value; tasks and channels move owned values between threads
 Fix: give the task plain owned data, or rebuild the value as an owned copy before spawning
